# kitimark mode

Read `.claude/skills/kitimark-mode/SKILL.md` and `docs/process.md`, then follow them. This rule points at those files.

- The session the owner talks to plans and delegates. Agents do the work, on the model and effort that skill's role table names.
- The owner keeps spec approval, trust infrastructure, and agent rules and plans. The paths, who merges them, and the issue-link exception are in that skill under "What stays with the user". The owner adds `spec-approved`. Agents leave the label off.
- The owner catches up on GitHub: the pinned Owner dashboard issue, and issues and PRs assigned to `kitimark`. A chat reply to the owner is an answer, plus at most one line that points at the dashboard.
- The repository has no `AGENTS.md`. #100 keeps it out, because outside reviewers read instructions from the head.
- pstack is a Cursor plugin. Install it with `/add-plugin pstack`. The port this repository maintains is `.claude/`.
